mystic models it. || BONUSES: the Mystic O.C.C.''s bonuses as production''s mystic stores them, plus +1 initiative, +2 roll with punch, +2 pull punch, +1 save vs Horror Factor (4+1=5 at level one) and +1 vs poison (toxins_poisons) and disease. || SKILLS: base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Dragonese is a named row at 90, per_level 0. Atlantean has no catalog row, so it is a pick from Language: Other at +40 (90%), as the Staphra Warrior and Warlord store it. Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic; Identify Plants & Fruits is Identify Plants & Fruit. The W.P. two of choice is a category pick. || HAND TO HAND: Basic granted; Expert for one related pick; Martial Arts and Assassin not offered. || RELATED and SECONDARY: five related at level one plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 13; two secondary at level one plus one at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 14 from the same list without bonuses. The Pilot exclusion (robots and power armor, tanks and APCs, any aircraft) uses the Staphra Warrior''s stored exclusion list. Wilderness Survival, printed under Electrical at +5%, is in the Wilderness category at the same +5%. || EQUIPMENT: catalog rows by slug; light body armor is mystic''s light-armor choice; ceremonial cloak and garments is ceremonial-robe, dagger is knife, belt with many pouches is utility-belt, notebook is note-pad. The weapon per W.P. is prose in restrictions. || MONEY: player characters 2D4x100 credits; slaves none, a restriction line. || PLAYER CHARACTER: the spy-or-renegade limit is the race''s, stated with the Staphra Warrior. || NOT STORED: height, weight, life span, habitat, slave market value (700,000 to 1.2 million credits), allies and enemies are in the body."
